<title>CHILE: Copec reports lower 9-month net.</title>
<headline>Copec reports lower 9-month net.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forestry and oil conglomerate Compania de Petroleos de Chile, or Copec, reported the following results in the first nine months of 1996 against the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>				9-mo 1996		9-mo 1995</p>
<p>Net profit		   77.46		    152.95</p>
<p>Operating profit	   17.49		     16.62</p>
<p>Non-operating profit     62.81		    138.72 Total</p>
<p>revenues		    468.69		    399.21</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in billions of pesos.</p>
<p>Copec is owned by Chile's Angelini Group and Carter Holt Harvey of New Zealand.</p>
<p>--Santiago newsroom +56-2-6995595 x211</p>
</text>
